course: dictionary
lesson: 10873
title: One word, two views
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Viewpoint is one of them. Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer wants. «A story told by a dog is not dumb: it shows the world from a new viewpoint.» The clue is story and the way of seeing the world, so here viewpoint means a way of thinking about something.
explain: «Example: a family in Colorado reaches a viewpoint with a fence.» Now the clues are reaches and fence. A family goes up to a place and stops at a fence to look out, so this viewpoint is a high place with a wide view.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the word. Does «a family reaches a way of thinking with a fence» make sense? No, so the second meaning is right. Phrases like «from my viewpoint» and «a different viewpoint» usually mean an opinion.
explain: Always check the clues before you choose. The same word can change its meaning with each sentence, and the context tells you which meaning to use.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Viewpoint» means a way of thinking about something, an opinion or point of view.
fact: «Viewpoint» can also mean a high place from which you can see a wide view, often with a sign or bench.
fact: Phrases such as «from my viewpoint» and «a different viewpoint» usually use the meaning about opinions.
fact: Animals can see things from a different viewpoint too: some bowerbirds arrange objects to change how big they look «from the female's viewpoint».
exercise: «A story told by a dog is not dumb: it shows the world from a new viewpoint.» What does viewpoint mean here? | A high place with a bench to sit on | *A way of thinking about something | A type of camera | A window in a house
exercise: «Example: a family in Colorado reaches a viewpoint with a fence.» What does viewpoint mean here? | An opinion about a story | *A high place with a wide view | A busy town square | A dark forest path
exercise: Which phrase tells you that viewpoint means an opinion? | *a different viewpoint | a high hill | a wide view | a sign on a bench
test: Leo reads, «We stopped at the viewpoint to look at the lake.» What does viewpoint mean here? | A way of thinking about the lake | A map of the town | A boat on the water | *A high place to see a wide view
test: Mia says, «From my viewpoint, we should go to the park.» What does viewpoint mean here? | A map of the town | *A way of thinking, an opinion | A high place with a bench | A park gate
exam: Which sentence uses viewpoint to mean a high place with a view? | «The story was told from a new viewpoint.» | «She gave a different viewpoint on the plan.» | «From my viewpoint, the film was too long.» | *«The car stopped at the viewpoint so we could see the valley.»
